{
  "summary": "Stops echoing input key material and unparsed descriptor strings in error messages produced during descriptor parsing, wallet imports, and transaction funding. Replaces raw key echoes with generic descriptions, caps echoed tokens at lengths too short to contain keys, and prints public representations via desc->ToString() when available. Updates existing functional and unit tests to reflect the modified error strings and adds test coverage verifying private keys are omitted from errors.",
  "problem": "Descriptor inputs can include secret material such as WIF private keys or extended private keys (xprvs). When descriptor parsing or derivation fails, current error messages quote the raw input strings directly, exposing private keys to application logs, exception reporters, or support screenshots.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Some descriptor error messages quote the string the caller sent, and a descriptor can hold a private key (a WIF, an xprv). The reply then carries the key into places the request may not go: an application's error log, an error reporter, a screenshot shared for help. Even the first characters of a key give away part of it.'",
    "Commit a3f26e8343: 'Error text is often logged or shared where the request is not. Even the first characters of a key give away part of it.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "No changes to the PR's contents; the patch is now provided where it was previously missing.",
  "card": "Prevents descriptor parsing and wallet RPC errors from echoing raw key material back to callers. Descriptors can contain private keys (WIF, xprv), and when parsing or derivation fails, current errors echo the input text, risking exposure in application logs, error aggregators, or screenshots. The change suppresses echoing raw key strings, restricts quoting of function names and path tokens to lengths that cannot fit key material, and prints sanitized public descriptors (desc->ToString()) where available. Tests are updated to assert the sanitized error messages and ensure no key prefixes leak.",
  "needs": [],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "medium",
    "touches": [
      "rpc_api",
      "wallet"
    ],
    "why": "Altering RPC error messages can break external scripts or wallet clients that rely on matching specific error string patterns."
  }
}
